9. CONNECTED DASHBOARDS AND DATA REFRESH
==================================================

All dashboards must read from the same authoritative database.

After a successful dataset import:
- Refresh the Data Manager's dataset and import history
- Refresh Energy Analyst metrics and charts
- Refresh area comparisons
- Recalculate high-consumption analysis
- Make updated findings available to the planner

After a planning action is saved:
- Refresh the planner's action list and dashboard metrics
- Ensure the action remains saved after page refresh

After an administrator changes permissions:
- Enforce the new permissions on subsequent backend requests

Use immediate UI refresh after successful writes and sensible
periodic polling if needed.

Display the latest successful refresh time.

Do not require WebSockets unless they are necessary and can
actually be implemented and tested.

Do not claim that the application has live electricity readings.

If no live energy source is connected, clearly label the data
as imported historical or sample data.

